{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And this is the matter of the release.</b> Even <b>the matter of the release</b> effects remission — if a person owes his fellow an oath, the seventh year remits it." "<b>Every creditor shall release his hand.</b> A loan is remitted, but not theft and not a deposit." "<b>He shall not press.</b> The creditor <b>shall not press his neighbor or his brother, for he has proclaimed</b> — the borrower — <b>release</b> for his fields, for the sake of Heaven, and he has nothing with which to repay, and he does not plant and does not harvest. But in other years a person plants and harvests, and if the creditor presses him, he says to him: wait for me until I sell my produce." "<b>For he has proclaimed release.</b> For the time of the release has arrived — like the language of מקרא קודש."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:52:52.191499278Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}